# GRID_AGENT_LOOP — feed the last line of this file to /loop:
#   /loop $(tail -1 GRID_AGENT_LOOP.sh)
Read docs/GRID_AGENT_CELL_ROADMAP.md and follow its doctrine and hard rules exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task in Section 6; the task's spec text is the requirement, the regression-table rows it names are the acceptance tests. TRUTH: never invent data, endpoints, or timings — read the actual anchors first (gridResearch.ts, gridTrace.ts, gridTrust.ts, gridTrustRunner.ts, GridView.tsx, gridRunStore.ts, gridStore.ts); the trace is a record never a performance (a step exists iff its call executed; failed steps show real errors; analyze consumes only successful steps' data); live-probe every endpoint before wiring a tool (curl, paste real response into Progress log) — dead endpoint = ledger note, never a mock in prod code. Reuse existing plumbing: runGridCell deps seam (tools are OPTIONAL deps members; absent tools = byte-identical current behavior, row 9), gridTrust bands unchanged (corroboration only appends reasons, row 10), cells JSONB additive (steps ≤12, meta ≤500 chars), reportQaGates house style (pure fn + numbered regression test); no parallel pipelines, no new npm deps (check package.json first), no Supabase client reads of financials/chunks. Only DeepSeek is a live LLM (ONE analyze call per cell max); Vercel Hobby 12-fn cap — any API route rides the existing [fn].ts dispatcher. A task is done only when: its numbered regression tests are green via npx vitest run (from apps/market-ui/), npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.app.json is 0 errors, ALL existing suites stayed green (gridTrust.test.ts, gridTrustRunner.test.ts, gridLessons.test.ts, gridRunStore.test.ts, EdgarLink.test.ts, gridResearch.sources.test.ts 37/37 via npx tsx), and vercel --prod from repo root ran IF UI changed. Then flip the ledger line to [x], append ONE Section 7 Progress-log line with REAL numbers (test counts, per-step ms from actual runs — no adjectives), and commit on roadmap/world-class with message "feat(grid-agent): AC-n <what> — <verify numbers>" (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). Never git push unless asked. PERSISTENCE: never end the loop on usage/rate limit or 429/overload — stop consuming tokens immediately, ScheduleWakeup 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger + Progress log and resume the same task from its last verified step; log partial progress BEFORE long/risky operations; chain hourly wakeups as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining in Section 6, or a task blocked on user-only input (credentials/infra) — then say exactly what's needed, ledger-note it, skip to the next unblocked [ ] task if one exists, and only if ALL remaining are blocked ScheduleWakeup 3600s so the loop resumes when unblocked.
